@@ -0,0 +1,98 @@
+# read_evm_call oracle service
+
+Generic **EVM state &rarr; Qubic** oracle. Given `(chainId, blockNumber, to, calldata)` it runs one
+read-only `eth_call` against that exact **finalized** block and returns the raw return data. Typical
+uses: `balanceOf`, `ownerOf`, `totalSupply`, reserve or price getters. No ABI is baked in: the
+querying Qubic smart contract encodes the call and decodes the result itself.
+
+It complements `read_evm_log`: that service proves something **happened** (an event), this one reads
+what something **is** at a fixed block.
+
+Implemented in Python (`read_evm_call_service.py`, stdlib only), with the same OM node <-> service
+framing and the same `EVM_RPC_URLS_<chainId>` configuration as `read_evm_log`.
+
+## Wire format
+
+Mirrors core's `OI::EvmCallRead` (`src/oracle_interfaces/EvmCallRead.h`, interface index 5).
+
+### Query — 568 bytes
+
+| offset | size | field         | notes                                                       |
+|-------:|-----:|---------------|-------------------------------------------------------------|
+| 0      | 8    | `chainId`     | uint64 LE                                                   |
+| 8      | 8    | `blockNumber` | uint64 LE; must be at or below the finalized head           |
+| 16     | 32   | `to`          | 20-byte address right-aligned; upper 12 bytes zero          |
+| 48     | 8    | `calldataLen` | uint64 LE, 4..512                                           |
+| 56     | 512  | `calldata`    | selector + ABI arguments; bytes beyond `calldataLen` zero   |
+
+### Reply — 568 bytes
+
+| offset | size | field       | notes                                                   |
+|-------:|-----:|-------------|---------------------------------------------------------|
+| 0      | 8    | `code`      | uint64 LE result code                                   |
+| 8      | 32   | `blockHash` | hash of the block that was read                         |
+| 40     | 8    | `reverted`  | 1 if the call reverted (data = revert data), else 0     |
+| 48     | 8    | `dataLen`   | 0..512                                                  |
+| 56     | 512  | `data`      | return or revert data, zero-padded                      |
+
+On any non-zero `code`, **all value fields are zero**.
+
+## Result codes
+
+| code | name                  | meaning                                                          |
+|-----:|-----------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------|
+| 0    | `SUCCESS`             | the call ran at the block; check `reverted`                      |
+| 1    | `BAD_QUERY`           | bad target word, `calldataLen` outside 4..512, dirty padding     |
+| 2    | `CHAIN_UNSUPPORTED`   | no RPC endpoints configured for `chainId`                        |
+| 3    | `BLOCK_NOT_FINALIZED` | block above the finalized head of some endpoint (retriable)      |
+| 4    | `BLOCK_TOO_OLD`       | more than 86,400 s before the finalized head (`STATE_WINDOW_SECONDS`) |
+| 5    | `OUT_OF_GAS`          | the call needed more than 10,000,000 gas                         |
+| 6    | `RETURN_TOO_LARGE`    | return or revert data over 512 bytes                             |
+
+A revert is a **result**, not a failure: `SUCCESS` with `reverted = 1` and the revert data. Other
+EVM execution failures (invalid opcode, bad jump, stack errors) are reported the same way with empty
+data. A transport error, an unrecognised node error or any provider disagreement is **not** a result
+code: the service abstains (oracle error flag, nothing committed).
+
+## Determinism guarantees
+
+- **Finalized only.** The block must be at or below the finalized head reported by *every*
+  endpoint (or `latest - EVM_MIN_CONFIRMATIONS_<chainId>` where configured).
+- **Pinned by hash.** The service resolves `blockNumber` to a block hash on every endpoint, requires
+  them to agree, then runs `eth_call` with an EIP-1898 block object
+  (`{"blockHash": ..., "requireCanonical": true}`), so all endpoints execute against the same state.
+- **Fixed call context.** Sender is the zero address, gas is exactly `GAS_CAP` (10,000,000), no
+  state overrides, no value.
+- **Multi-provider byte-agreement** on the block and on the normalized outcome
+  (return data / revert data / out of gas); otherwise abstain.
+- **State window, not archive nodes.** Endpoints need about a day of state, not full archive
+  history.
+
+## Config
+
+| env var                             | purpose                                                          |
+|-------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------|
+| `READ_EVM_CALL_SERVICE_HOST/PORT`   | interface slot the OM node reaches this service on (default port 9007) |
+| `EVM_RPC_URLS_<chainId>`            | shared with `read_evm_log`; endpoints must support EIP-1898      |
+| `EVM_MIN_CONFIRMATIONS_<chainId>`   | optional; `latest - N` instead of the `finalized` tag            |
+
+Run: `python3 read_evm_call_service.py` (Python 3.8+, no third-party packages).
+
+## Tests
+
+```bash
+python3 test/mock_evm_rpc.py --port 18645 &
+python3 test/mock_evm_rpc.py --port 18646 &
+python3 test/mock_evm_rpc.py --port 18647 --tamper &
+python3 test/selftest.py     # exit 0 = all scenarios pass (29 checks)
+```
+
+The mock node only answers `eth_call` when the service sends the exact required context (zero
+sender, `GAS_CAP`, EIP-1898 hash pin), so the selftest also checks the call the service makes.
+
+Against real endpoints (nothing is sent to Qubic):
+
+```bash
+EVM_RPC_URLS_8453=https://base-rpc.publicnode.com,https://mainnet.base.org \
+python3 test/live_check.py 8453 0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913 0x<holder>
+```
diff --git a/oracles/read_evm_call/read_evm_call_service.py b/oracles/read_evm_call/read_evm_call_service.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..884d533
--- /dev/null
+++ b/oracles/read_evm_call/read_evm_call_service.py
@@ -0,0 +1,328 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env python3
+"""read_evm_call oracle service (interface index 5): read EVM contract state at a finalized block.
+
+Query 568B: chainId u64 | blockNumber u64 | to 32B | calldataLen u64 | calldata 512B.
+Reply 568B: code u64 | blockHash 32B | reverted u64 | dataLen u64 | data 512B.
+Only finalized blocks are read; every configured RPC endpoint must agree byte-for-byte on the block
+and on the call's outcome, otherwise the service abstains (oracle error flag, no reply payload).
+
+Speaks the OM node <-> service protocol of oracles/core/base_oracle_service.cpp (same framing as
+read_evm_log):
+  query:  header 8B (size LE24 | type=190 | dejavu u32) | OracleMachineQuery 16B | payload 568B
+  reply:  header 8B (size LE24 | type=191 | dejavu=0)   | OracleMachineReply 16B | payload 568B
+
+Env: READ_EVM_CALL_SERVICE_PORT (default 9007), EVM_RPC_URLS_<chainId> (comma-separated; the same
+variables as read_evm_log), EVM_MIN_CONFIRMATIONS_<chainId> (optional: latest-N instead of the
+"finalized" tag).
+"""
+
+import json
+import os
+import signal
+import socket
+import socketserver
+import struct
+import sys
+import urllib.error
+import urllib.request
+
+QUERY_SIZE = 568
+REPLY_SIZE = 568
+DATA_CAPACITY = 512
+OM_QUERY_TYPE = 190
+OM_REPLY_TYPE = 191
+MAX_RPC_RESPONSE_BYTES = 8 * 1024 * 1024
+RPC_TIMEOUT_S = 10
+SOCKET_TIMEOUT_S = 600  # mirrors core's BaseOracleService::TIME_OUT_MS
+MAX_FRAME_BYTES = 4096  # larger frame means corrupt framing, not an unrelated message
+
+# Mirrors core's OI::EvmCallRead
+GAS_CAP = 10_000_000
+STATE_WINDOW_SECONDS = 86_400
+ZERO_ADDRESS = "0x" + "00" * 20
+
+# Result codes (mirror core's OI::EvmCallRead)
+SUCCESS = 0
+BAD_QUERY = 1
+CHAIN_UNSUPPORTED = 2
+BLOCK_NOT_FINALIZED = 3
+BLOCK_TOO_OLD = 4
+OUT_OF_GAS = 5
+RETURN_TOO_LARGE = 6
+
+# Oracle error flags (mirror core's network_messages/common_def.h)
+NO_ERROR = 0x0
+ORACLE_UNAVAIL = 0x2
+INVALID_ARG = 0x10
+
+SUPPORTED_CHAIN_IDS = [1, 10, 56, 137, 250, 8453, 43114, 42161, 11155111]
+INTERFACE_INDEX = 5
+
+# EVM execution failures other than out-of-gas. They consume the call and return no data, so they
+# are reported like a revert with empty data. Messages are matched case-insensitively; any error not
+# recognised here makes the service abstain rather than guess.
+VM_FAILURE_MARKERS = (
+    "invalid opcode",
+    "invalid jump destination",
+    "stack underflow",
+    "stack overflow",
+    "write protection",
+    "return data out of bounds",
+)
+
+
+class Abstain(Exception):
+    """Transport error, malformed data or provider disagreement: commit nothing."""
+
+
+def hexb(s):
+    """0x-prefixed hex string -> bytes; raises on anything else."""
+    if not isinstance(s, str) or not s.startswith("0x") or len(s) % 2:
+        raise Abstain(f"expected 0x-prefixed even-length hex, got {s!r}")
+    try:
+        return bytes.fromhex(s[2:])
+    except ValueError as e:
+        raise Abstain(f"bad hex: {e}") from e
+
+
+def load_chains():
+    chains = {}
+    for chain_id in SUPPORTED_CHAIN_IDS:
+        urls = os.environ.get(f"EVM_RPC_URLS_{chain_id}", "")
+        endpoints = [u.strip() for u in urls.split(",") if u.strip()]
+        if not endpoints:
+            continue
+        conf = os.environ.get(f"EVM_MIN_CONFIRMATIONS_{chain_id}", "")
+        chains[chain_id] = {
+            "endpoints": endpoints,
+            "min_confirmations": max(0, int(conf)) if conf else 0,
+        }
+    return chains
+
+
+def rpc_raw(endpoint, method, params):
+    """One JSON-RPC call; returns the decoded reply object (with "result" or "error")."""
+    body = json.dumps({"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "method": method, "params": params}).encode()
+    req = urllib.request.Request(endpoint, data=body, headers={"Content-Type": "application/json"})
+    try:
+        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=RPC_TIMEOUT_S) as resp:
+            raw = resp.read(MAX_RPC_RESPONSE_BYTES + 1)
+    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:  # some providers send JSON-RPC errors with HTTP 4xx/5xx
+        raw = e.read(MAX_RPC_RESPONSE_BYTES + 1)
+    except Exception as e:
+        raise Abstain(f"transport: {e}") from e
+    if len(raw) > MAX_RPC_RESPONSE_BYTES:
+        raise Abstain("response too large")
+    try:
+        reply = json.loads(raw)
+    except ValueError as e:
+        raise Abstain(f"bad json: {e}") from e
+    if not isinstance(reply, dict) or ("result" not in reply and "error" not in reply):
+        raise Abstain("not a JSON-RPC reply")
+    return reply
+
+
+def rpc(endpoint, method, params):
+    reply = rpc_raw(endpoint, method, params)
+    if "result" not in reply or reply.get("error"):
+        raise Abstain(f"rpc error: {reply.get('error')}")
+    return reply["result"]
+
+
+def block_info(block):
+    if not isinstance(block, dict):
+        raise Abstain("block not returned")
+    return int(block["number"], 16), hexb(block["hash"]), int(block["timestamp"], 16)
+
+
+def finalized_head(endpoint, chain):
+    """(number, timestamp) of the block this endpoint treats as final."""
+    if chain["min_confirmations"]:
+        latest = rpc(endpoint, "eth_getBlockByNumber", ["latest", False])
+        number = int(latest["number"], 16) - chain["min_confirmations"]
+        block = rpc(endpoint, "eth_getBlockByNumber", [hex(number), False])
+    else:
+        block = rpc(endpoint, "eth_getBlockByNumber", ["finalized", False])
+    number, _, timestamp = block_info(block)
+    return number, timestamp
+
+
+def call_outcome(endpoint, to20, calldata, block_hash):
+    """Normalized outcome of one eth_call pinned to block_hash (EIP-1898)."""
+    call = {"from": ZERO_ADDRESS, "to": "0x" + to20.hex(), "gas": hex(GAS_CAP), "data": "0x" + calldata.hex()}
+    reply = rpc_raw(endpoint, "eth_call", [call, {"blockHash": "0x" + block_hash.hex(), "requireCanonical": True}])
+    error = reply.get("error")
+    if not error:
+        return ("ok", hexb(reply["result"]))
+    if not isinstance(error, dict):
+        raise Abstain(f"malformed error: {error!r}")
+    message = str(error.get("message", "")).lower()
+    if error.get("code") == 3 or message.startswith("execution reverted"):
+        data = error.get("data")
+        return ("revert", hexb(data) if isinstance(data, str) and data else b"")
+    if "out of gas" in message:
+        return ("oog", b"")
+    if any(marker in message for marker in VM_FAILURE_MARKERS):
+        return ("revert", b"")
+    raise Abstain(f"unrecognised call error: {error}")
+
+
+def read_call(chain, block_number, to20, calldata):
+    """Returns (code, block_hash, outcome) agreed by every endpoint, or raises Abstain."""
+    agreed_block = None
+    outcome = None
+    too_old = False
+    for endpoint in chain["endpoints"]:
+        head_number, head_time = finalized_head(endpoint, chain)
+        if block_number > head_number:
+            return BLOCK_NOT_FINALIZED, None, None
+        block = block_info(rpc(endpoint, "eth_getBlockByNumber", [hex(block_number), False]))
+        if block[0] != block_number:
+            raise Abstain("endpoint returned a different block number")
+        if agreed_block is None:
+            agreed_block = block
+        elif block != agreed_block:
+            raise Abstain("provider disagreement on block")
+        if head_time - block[2] > STATE_WINDOW_SECONDS:
+            too_old = True
+    if too_old:
+        return BLOCK_TOO_OLD, None, None
+    for endpoint in chain["endpoints"]:
+        one = call_outcome(endpoint, to20, calldata, agreed_block[1])
+        if outcome is None:
+            outcome = one
+        elif one != outcome:
+            raise Abstain("provider disagreement on call result")
+    return SUCCESS, agreed_block[1], outcome
+
+
+def code_reply(code):
+    return struct.pack("<Q", code) + bytes(REPLY_SIZE - 8)
+
+
+def handle_query(chains, payload):
+    """568B query payload -> (errorFlags, 568B reply payload). Abstains via non-zero flags."""
+    if len(payload) != QUERY_SIZE:
+        return INVALID_ARG, bytes(REPLY_SIZE)
+    chain_id, block_number, to_word, calldata_len, calldata = struct.unpack("<QQ32sQ512s", payload)
+
+    if (to_word[:12] != bytes(12) or to_word[12:] == bytes(20)
+            or not 4 <= calldata_len <= 512 or calldata[calldata_len:] != bytes(512 - calldata_len)):
+        return NO_ERROR, code_reply(BAD_QUERY)
+    if chain_id not in chains:
+        return NO_ERROR, code_reply(CHAIN_UNSUPPORTED)
+
+    try:
+        code, block_hash, outcome = read_call(chains[chain_id], block_number, to_word[12:], calldata[:calldata_len])
+    except Exception as e:  # Abstain, or a malformed field (KeyError/ValueError) from a provider
+        print(f"[ReadEvmCall] abstain: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
+        return ORACLE_UNAVAIL, bytes(REPLY_SIZE)
+
+    if code != SUCCESS:
+        return NO_ERROR, code_reply(code)
+    kind, data = outcome
+    if kind == "oog":
+        return NO_ERROR, code_reply(OUT_OF_GAS)
+    if len(data) > DATA_CAPACITY:
+        return NO_ERROR, code_reply(RETURN_TOO_LARGE)
+    if len(block_hash) != 32:
+        return ORACLE_UNAVAIL, bytes(REPLY_SIZE)
+
+    reply = struct.pack("<Q", SUCCESS) + block_hash
+    reply += struct.pack("<QQ", 1 if kind == "revert" else 0, len(data))
+    reply += data + bytes(DATA_CAPACITY - len(data))
+    assert len(reply) == REPLY_SIZE
+    return NO_ERROR, reply
+
+
+def recv_exact(sock, n):
+    buf = b""
+    while len(buf) < n:
+        chunk = sock.recv(n - len(buf))
+        if not chunk:
+            return None
+        buf += chunk
+    return buf
+
+
+class Handler(socketserver.BaseRequestHandler):
+    def setup(self):
+        self.request.settimeout(SOCKET_TIMEOUT_S)
+
+    def handle(self):
+        try:
+            self.serve()
+        except socket.timeout:
+            return  # idle too long; the node reconnects
+
+    def serve(self):
+        while True:
+            header = recv_exact(self.request, 8)
+            if header is None:
+                return
+            size = header[0] | (header[1] << 8) | (header[2] << 16)
+            msg_type = header[3]
+            if size < 8 or size > MAX_FRAME_BYTES:
+                return  # corrupt framing: cannot resync, drop the connection
+            body = recv_exact(self.request, size - 8)
+            if body is None:
+                return
+            if msg_type != OM_QUERY_TYPE or len(body) != 16 + QUERY_SIZE:
+                continue  # skip unrelated frames
+            query_id, interface_index = struct.unpack("<QI", body[:12])
+            if interface_index != INTERFACE_INDEX:
+                continue  # not our interface (misrouted config)
+            try:
+                flags, reply_payload = handle_query(self.server.chains, body[16:])
+            except Exception as e:  # structural backstop: never kill the OM connection
+                print(f"[ReadEvmCall] abstain (unexpected): {e}", file=sys.stderr)
+                flags, reply_payload = ORACLE_UNAVAIL, bytes(REPLY_SIZE)
+
+            reply_size = 8 + 16 + REPLY_SIZE
+            packet = bytes([reply_size & 0xFF, (reply_size >> 8) & 0xFF,
+                            (reply_size >> 16) & 0xFF, OM_REPLY_TYPE]) + bytes(4)
+            packet += struct.pack("<QH6x", query_id, flags)
+            packet += reply_payload
+            self.request.sendall(packet)
+
+
+class Server(socketserver.ThreadingTCPServer):
+    allow_reuse_address = True
+    daemon_threads = True
+
+
+def main():
+    args = sys.argv[1:]
+    if args[:1] == ["--log"] and len(args) == 2:
+        log = open(args[1], "a", buffering=1)
+        sys.stdout = sys.stderr = log
+    elif args:
+        print(f"usage: {sys.argv[0]} [--log FILE]")
+        return 0 if args[:1] == ["--help"] else 1
+
+    signal.signal(signal.SIGTERM, lambda *_: sys.exit(0))
+    urllib.request.install_opener(urllib.request.build_opener(urllib.request.ProxyHandler({})))
+    chains = load_chains()
+    if not chains:
+        print("No chains configured! Set EVM_RPC_URLS_<chainId>.", file=sys.stderr)
+        return 1
+    port = int(os.environ.get("READ_EVM_CALL_SERVICE_PORT", "9007"))
+    for chain_id, chain in chains.items():
+        finality = (f"{chain['min_confirmations']} confirmations"
+                    if chain["min_confirmations"] else '"finalized" tag')
+        print(f"[ReadEvmCall] chain {chain_id}: {len(chain['endpoints'])} endpoint(s), {finality}")
+    server = Server(("0.0.0.0", port), Handler)
+    server.chains = chains
+    print(f"[ReadEvmCall] listening on {port}")
+    try:
+        server.serve_forever()
+    except KeyboardInterrupt:
+        pass
+    finally:
+        server.server_close()
+        print("[ReadEvmCall] shutdown")
+    return 0
+
+
+if __name__ == "__main__":
+    sys.exit(main())
